Week 4 Project Report

Project Title

Chicken Cross Road Game (Java)

Week 4: Vehicle System Implementation

Objective

The objective of Week 4 was to implement a vehicle system by adding moving obstacles (cars), handling collision detection, and improving the overall gameplay.

Activities Completed

- Created the Car class to represent moving vehicles.
- Implemented continuous car movement across the road.
- Added multiple cars with different starting positions.
- Assigned different speeds to each car.
- Assigned different colors to each car to represent multiple vehicle types.
- Increased the road width to provide better movement space.
- Adjusted the player's starting position to the middle grass field.
- Improved tree placement for a better game environment.
- Implemented collision detection between the player and vehicles.
- Reset the player to the starting position after a collision.
- Removed one unnecessary vehicle to avoid overlapping and improve gameplay.

Problems Faced

- The "Vehicle.java" file showed compilation errors while implementing the vehicle system.
- Some vehicles overlapped because they were moving in the same lane.
- The road width was too small at first.
- The player's starting position was not properly aligned.

Solutions

- Used the existing Car class instead of the "Vehicle" class.
- Changed vehicle positions and speeds to reduce overlapping.
- Increased the road width.
- Repositioned the player and trees for better game balance.

Deliverables

- Car.java
- Updated GamePanel.java
- Vehicle movement system
- Collision detection system
- Multiple colored vehicles with different speeds

Expected Outcome

- Vehicles move continuously across the road.
- Each vehicle has a different speed and color.
- The player resets after colliding with a vehicle.
- The game environment is more organized and visually improved.

Conclusion

Week 4 was completed successfully. The vehicle movement, collision detection, and multiple vehicle implementation were finished, making the game more interactive and closer to the original Chicken Cross Road gameplay.